---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CLARITY_ID, CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host and reuse`} description="Legal notice of Term Dates Finder: the publisher Radif Partners, the host, what the school calendars are for, limits of liability, reuse of council data under the Open Government Licence." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Hosting provider</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
    <p>The site republishes the school term and holiday dates set by local authorities in England, Scotland and Wales and the common closure dates of Northern Ireland, with free tools to check a date, count days and compare two areas. It is independent and has no link with any council, the Department for Education, the Scottish or Welsh Government or the Department of Education in Northern Ireland. A school may set dates that differ from its council's: the school's own calendar prevails. Method: <a href={route('method', lang)}>how the dates are checked</a>.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Each date is read on the official page shown with it and tested by software, without any guarantee that no error or late change remains. The publisher cannot be held liable for a booking, a missed day or an absence penalty based only on this site. Errors can be reported on the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property and reuse</h2>
    <p>Texts, graphics and code belong to the publisher. Term dates published by councils, GOV.UK bank holiday data and legislation are public sector information reused under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>, with the source named on each page.</p>
    {/* gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Personal data and cookies</h2>
    {GA4_ID ? (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser. The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, 13 months at most), with no advertising{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. Details, legal basis and how to object: <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>) : (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser and the site sets no cookies{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. See the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>)}
    {/* /gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, with the page address and the reason.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law. Failing an amicable solution, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without prejudice to the mandatory rules protecting consumers in their country of residence. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
